  "aggregate_rule": "Per system and language, the unweighted mean of the per-category accuracies (correct / n) over the categories run, each category counting once whatever its n, which is recorded beside it; per group the same over the group's categories; over both languages the same over every (language, category) pair. correct and n are the score file's correct_count and total_count: for normal_multi_turn_* they count single answers, while ACEBench's own accuracy there (acebench_accuracy) counts a turn right only when all its answers are. ACEBench's own Summary is not used: it weights normal, special and agent and counts the agent categories, not run, as 0.",
  "format_rule": "Per category: n answers; tool_call, the answers holding <tool_call> (the fine-tuned model's trained format); acebench_format, the answers whose first outermost [...] parses as a Python list of calls, as ACEBench's parser takes them ([ApiName(key='value')]). An answer may be counted in both or in neither; special categories ask for text.",
